[
  {
    "name": "Task 1: Create Performance Monitoring Module and Class",
    "description": "Create a new Python module named `codx.junior.monitoring`. Inside this module, implement a class called `PerformanceMonitor`. This class will be responsible for managing the Py-spy monitoring process, including starting and stopping recordings. Ensure that the class has methods to handle these operations and any necessary state management (e.g., tracking if monitoring is currently active)."
  },
  {
    "name": "Task 2: Implement `/performance/start-monitoring` Endpoint",
    "description": "Integrate a new API endpoint `/performance/start-monitoring` into the FastAPI application. This endpoint should only be accessible to users with administrator privileges. Upon a successful request:\n1. Obtain the current process ID (PID) using `os.getpid()`.\n2. Start Py-spy monitoring on the obtained PID. The output should be directed to an SVG file.\n3. Define the output directory for SVG files as `images/monitoring`. Ensure this directory exists. If it doesn't, create it.\n4. Generate a timestamped filename for the SVG file (e.g., `monitoring_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.svg`).\n5. Save the generated SVG file in the `images/monitoring` directory.\n6. Implement robust error handling for cases where `py-spy` is not installed or if there are issues creating the output directory or saving the file."
  },
  {
    "name": "Task 3: Implement `/performance/end-monitoring` Endpoint",
    "description": "Integrate a new API endpoint `/performance/end-monitoring` into the FastAPI application. This endpoint should also be restricted to administrator users.\n\nUpon a successful request:\n1. Stop the ongoing Py-spy recording.\n2. Ensure that any resources associated with the monitoring process are properly cleaned up.\n3. Provide appropriate feedback to the client indicating that monitoring has been stopped."
  },
  {
    "name": "Task 4: Ensure Directory Existence and Configuration",
    "description": "Before starting any monitoring, verify that the `images/monitoring` directory exists. If it does not exist, create it.\n\nAdditionally, ensure that the `CODX_JUNIOR_STATIC_FOLDER` environment variable is correctly configured and accessible, as this variable is used to determine the base path for saving the monitoring SVG files. If this environment variable is not set, the application should handle this gracefully, potentially by raising an error or using a default path, though using the environment variable is preferred as per the requirements."
  },
  {
    "name": "Task 5: Integrate and Test Endpoints",
    "description": "Add the newly created `PerformanceMonitor` class and its associated endpoints to the main FastAPI application.\n\nThoroughly test the following:\n- The `/performance/start-monitoring` endpoint to ensure it starts recording, generates an SVG file in the correct location with a timestamped name, and is protected by admin access control.\n- The `/performance/end-monitoring` endpoint to confirm it stops the recording and is also protected by admin access control.\n- Verify that Py-spy is correctly installed and functional within the environment.\n- Test error handling scenarios, such as attempting to start monitoring when Py-spy is not installed or when the output directory cannot be created."
  }
]
```
